      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "certiorari to the united states court of appeals for the ninth circuit No. 20\u2013828. Argued November 8, 2021\u2014Decided March 4, 2022"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents interpret \u00a7 1806(f) more broadly, arguing that it also can be triggered when a civil litigant seeks to obtain secret surveillance information, as respondents did here, and when the Government moves to dismiss a case pursuant to the state secrets privilege."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0000-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We now hold that \u00a7 1806(f) has no such effect, and we therefore reverse."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0000-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents Yassir Fazaga, Ali Malik, and Yasser Abdel Rahim are members of Muslim communities in southern California who claim that the Federal Bureau of Investigation illegally surveilled them because of their religion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0001-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit denied rehearing en banc over the dissent of Judge Bumatay and nine other judges. We granted certiorari to decide whether \u00a7 1806(f) displaces the state secrets privilege."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government contends that the Ninth Circuit erred because \u00a7 1806(f) is \u201c `relevant only when a litigant challenges the admissibility of the government's surveillance evidence.' \u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents do not dispute that \u00a7 1806(f) applies when the Government seeks to introduce evidence and a private party seeks to prevent such use, but they argue that \u00a7 1806(f) is also sometimes triggered when \u201ca civil litigant seeks to obtain such secret information.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In respondents' view, the attempt to leverage a claim of privilege into a dismissal constitutes a \u201cuse\u201d of FISA information against them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government disagrees with both of these theories. It argues that the assertion of the state secrets privilege did not constitute a \u201cuse\u201d of \u201cinformation obtained or derived from an electronic surveillance.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-828",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57ea5d9bc577453e7df11fc4173900104e1d10f11d50c1ebfc1be0bd4bc6fc5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57ea5d9bc577-0001-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We need not resolve this dispute about the meaning of \u00a7 1806(f) because we reverse the Ninth Circuit on an alternative ground\u2014namely, that even as interpreted by respondents, \u00a7 1806(f) does not displace the state secrets privilege."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
